From fe7e6f6a3c50f6cc947e2b2f3e3d5ad96cb2caf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:20:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(@wdio/config): resolve --spec glob patterns from the
 current working directory

The docs say a `--spec` path is resolved from the current working
directory. That was true for a file, but a glob pattern with a directory
was kept relative and globbed from the directory of the config file. With
the config in a sub folder, `--spec ./specs/*.js` found nothing while
`--spec ./specs/login.js` worked, and the glob needed `../specs/*.js`
instead.

`makeRelativeToCWD` now resolves every `--spec` value with a directory
from the current working directory, also a glob pattern. A value without
a directory (`login`, `*.e2e.js`) still matches spec files by name.

A CLI file that `isFile()` finds relative to the current working
directory is now also made absolute from there, not from the config
directory, so a bare file name of the working directory points to the
right file.

The v10 migration guide and the migration skill describe the change.

Fix #14447
